//! # A tour of Moddil
//!
//! `shorty` is a link shortener with two endpoints:
//!
//! - `POST /links` with `{"url": "https://…"}` stores the link and answers `201 {"code": "…"}`;
//! - `GET /{code}` answers with a redirect, or `404`.
//!
//! It is small, but it touches most of the language: validated types, typed errors that must be
//! handled, a user-defined effect with two handlers, root capabilities, structured concurrency
//! with isolation, graceful shutdown, and tests that run against a simulated network.
//!
//! Read the modules in order: [`types`], [`links`], [`routes`], [`serve`], then `main`
//! (`src/main.moddil`). The standard mods it uses are written in Moddil and named through the
//! umbrella mod (`mods/moddil`); its tests run natively, on the interpreter and as WASM
//! (`specs/tour.md`: From markdown to source).

pub use mod::types::{Code, Target, LinkError};
pub use mod::links::{Links, MemoryLinks};
pub use mod::routes::app;
